{
  "an5.73:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 5.73 ",
  "an5.73:0.2": "8. Warriors ",
  "an5.73:0.3": "One Who Lives by the Teaching (1st) ",
  "an5.73:1.1": "Then a mendicant went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "an5.73:1.2": "“Sir, they speak of ‘one who lives by the teaching’. ",
  "an5.73:1.3": "How is a mendicant who lives by the teaching defined?” ",
  "an5.73:2.1": "“Mendicant, take a mendicant who memorizes the teaching—",
  "an5.73:2.2": "statements, mixed prose & verse, discussions, verses, inspired exclamations, legends, stories of past lives, amazing stories, and elaborations. ",
  "an5.73:2.3": "They spend too much time studying that teaching. They neglect retreat, and are not committed to internal serenity of heart. ",
  "an5.73:2.4": "That mendicant is called one who studies a lot, not one who lives by the teaching. ",
  "an5.73:3.1": "Furthermore, a mendicant teaches Dhamma in detail to others as they learned and memorized it. ",
  "an5.73:3.2": "They spend too much time advocating that teaching. They neglect retreat, and are not committed to internal serenity of heart. ",
  "an5.73:3.3": "That mendicant is called one who advocates a lot, not one who lives by the teaching. ",
  "an5.73:4.1": "Furthermore, a mendicant rehearses the teaching in detail as they learned and memorized it. ",
  "an5.73:4.2": "They spend too much time reciting that teaching. They neglect retreat, and are not committed to internal serenity of heart. ",
  "an5.73:4.3": "That mendi